{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.DeckRealityEquivariance","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DeckRealityEquivariance","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Matrix.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Complex.Basic"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DeckRealityEquivariance.deck_eigenspace_exchange","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DeckRealityEquivariance.deck_eigenspace_exchange","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DeckRealityEquivariance.lean#L72-L87","doc":"**Deck eigenspace exchange (the ρ-equivariance, proved).** For a real\ndeck matrix `U`, conjugation carries the `i`-eigenspace to the\n`(−i)`-eigenspace and back — `F∘ρ = conj∘F` at the eigenspace level for the\nT1 cover's deck action (multipliers ±i, derived in T1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DeckRealityEquivariance.conj_eigenvector_of_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DeckRealityEquivariance.conj_eigenvector_of_real","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DeckRealityEquivariance.lean#L59-L70","doc":"**Conjugate eigenvectors of a real operator.** If `U` is real\n(`U.map star = U`) and `U·v = μ·v`, then `U·(star v) = (conj μ)·(star v)`:\nthe complex eigenspaces of a real operator come in conjugate pairs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DeckRealityEquivariance.mulVec_map_star","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DeckRealityEquivariance.mulVec_map_star","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DeckRealityEquivariance.lean#L51-L57","doc":"Entrywise conjugation intertwines matrix action:\n`star (U·v) = (U.map star)·(star v)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}